# Yool AI Plugin — Cursor Rules
# This file is automatically injected into every Composer session.
# Read it fully before writing any code.

## Project Overview

**Name**: Yool AI Plugin — Enterprise Lecture Reference Framework  
**Type**: Production-grade SaaS microservices platform  
**Goal**: A passive recording and content-tracking tool that lets an institution see, for every lecture delivered, exactly which topics the professor covered and when — with near-zero effort from the professor.  
**Deployment**: Docker Compose, self-hosted, HTTPS via nginx.

### One-line pitch
The admin creates courses and assigns teachers. The teacher opens the app, taps Start, teaches, taps Stop. The system transcribes the audio and generates a structured topic outline. The admin can then browse and search across all sessions to audit what was covered.

---

## Architecture

```
Client (HTTPS)
    │
    ▼
nginx (reverse proxy, TLS termination, rate limiting, structured JSON logs)
    │
    ├──► auth    (port 8001) — authentication, RBAC, teacher/admin management
    ├──► session (port 8002) — courses, live sessions (admin creates, teacher records)
    ├──► stt     (port 8003) — speech-to-text WebSocket stream + topic outline generation
    └──► query   (port 8004) — semantic search across topic outlines and transcripts
    
Infrastructure:
    PostgreSQL  — shared relational DB (all services share one DB via shared/models/)
    Redis       — JWT blocklist + sliding window rate limiting
```

---

## User Roles & Flows

### Roles (3 total — NO students)

```
SUPER_ADMIN  → full system access, can create any role
ADMIN        → manage users, create courses, assign teachers, review topic outlines
TEACHER      → picks a course, taps Start, teaches, taps Stop. That's it.
```

**There are NO student accounts. The platform is purely enterprise-internal.**

### Teacher UX (3 taps, total)

1. Open the app → see "your courses today"
2. Pick a course
3. Tap **Start lecture**

The session auto-titles itself (e.g. "Cours: Algorithmes — 30/04/2026 10:00"), records audio, transcribes in real time. The teacher taps **Stop** when done — there is no automatic stop, no silence detection, and no max-duration cap.

### Admin UX

- Creates courses, assigns each course to a teacher
- Reviews structured topic outlines for every recorded session
- Searches across all sessions ("in which lecture did Prof. X cover dynamic programming?")

### What the institution gets back

For every recorded lecture, a structured topic outline:

```json
{
  "teacher": "Prof. Benmoussa",
  "course": "Algorithmes et Structures de Données",
  "date": "2026-04-30",
  "topics": [
    {
      "start_time": "00:00:00",
      "end_time":   "00:18:30",
      "title":      "Introduction et rappels sur la récursion",
      "description":"Le professeur a rappelé la définition de la récursion et présenté deux exemples : factorielle et Fibonacci.",
      "key_concepts": ["récursion", "factorielle", "Fibonacci", "cas de base"]
    },
    {
      "start_time": "00:18:30",
      "end_time":   "00:42:00",
      "title":      "Complexité et débordement de pile",
      "description":"Discussion sur la complexité O(2^n) de la version naïve de Fibonacci et le risque de stack overflow.",
      "key_concepts": ["complexité", "stack overflow", "mémoïsation"]
    }
  ],
  "language": "fr",
  "duration_minutes": 75
}
```

