## What was removed (old → new)

| Removed | Replaced by |
|---------|-------------|
| Student accounts and enrollment | Nothing — institution is the audience |
| Class-link invites, student registration | Nothing |
| Student-style summaries (key_points, quiz, glossary, qa_pairs) | Chronological topic outline with timestamps |
| Per-session consent dialog | Institutional consent recorded once at org level |
| Teacher creates own courses | Admin creates and assigns courses |
| Manual session create + title + start + end | Single Start tap; auto-title; manual Stop |
| PartialSummary (live catch-up for students) | Nothing |
| Enrollment model | Deleted |
| CourseInvite model | Deleted |

---

## Tech Stack (non-negotiable, do not deviate)

- **Framework**: FastAPI (async only — every DB/Redis call must be awaited)
- **ORM**: SQLAlchemy 2.x async (`AsyncSession`, `select()`, not `session.query()`)
- **Validation**: Pydantic v2 (`model_config`, `field_validator`, `Field(...)` constraints)
- **Migrations**: Alembic — sequential numbered files: `001_...`, `002_...` (currently at `007`, next is `008`)
- **Logging**: `structlog` — structured key=value, never `print()` or `logging.basicConfig()`
- **Auth**: RS256 JWTs (asymmetric — private key in auth only, public key shareable)
- **Passwords**: bcrypt via `core.security.hash_password()` — never roll your own
- **Redis client**: `redis.asyncio` (aioredis pattern)
- **Styling**: Python 3.11+, type-annotated throughout (`Annotated[X, Depends()]`)

